Cooperation requires the participation of another party, specifically,
the DevTeam. If you don't have any suggestions as to how to get that
participation --- and it doesn't seem like you do --- then competition
would be the only way you would have available to you. The DevTeam does
make some resources available to you, even as a competitor, on the open
internet: various RGRN posts, the bug list (although yes, patches would
be nice), and development tools like the "this is how to build it under
Microsoft Visual Studio" kit.

My informed guess --- though obviously I can't say for sure --- is that
if you were to actually end up in competition by working on a variant,
you would get additional private resources from the DevTeam. Presumably,
you'd be running into bugs, fixing bugs, and sending back what you
were doing; I would find it difficult to imagine the DevTeam completely
ignoring you in return. But complaining that they aren't cooperating?
